* 16 Power BI measures for the Channel Health Dashboard.
* Stored in a dedicated _Measures table. Model: star schema.
* DIM_DATE marked as date table, single-direction relationships.

1. Channel: sell-in, sell-through, inventory
Sell-Through Units = SUM ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[UNITS_SOLD] )
Sell-In Units = SUM ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[UNITS_SELL_IN] )
Sell-In to Sell-Through = DIVIDE ( [Sell-In Units], [Sell-Through Units] )

Inventory is semi-additive: sum across distributors/parts, but take the LAST week, never sum across weeks
Channel Inventory Units =
VAR LastWeek = MAX ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[WEEK_START] )
RETURN CALCULATE ( SUM ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[UNITS_ON_HAND] ), VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[WEEK_START] = LastWeek )

POS 13wk Avg Units =
VAR LastWeek = MAX ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[WEEK_START] )
RETURN CALCULATE ( SUM ( VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[POS_13WK_AVG] ), VW_CHANNEL_WEEKLY[WEEK_START] = LastWeek )

Weeks of Inventory = DIVIDE ( [Channel Inventory Units], [POS 13wk Avg Units] )
WOI Target = 10
WOI vs Target = [Weeks of Inventory] - [WOI Target]

2. Bookings and billings
Bookings = SUM ( VW_BOOKINGS[BOOKING_VALUE] )
Billings = SUM ( VW_BILLINGS[AMOUNT] )
Book-to-Bill = DIVIDE ( [Bookings], [Billings] )
Billings PQ = CALCULATE ( [Billings], DATEADD ( DIM_DATE[DATE], -1, QUARTER ) )
Billings QoQ % = DIVIDE ( [Billings] - [Billings PQ], [Billings PQ] )

3.  Backlog (current snapshot, intentionally not related to DIM_DATE)
Open Backlog $ = SUM ( VW_BACKLOG_CURRENT[OPEN_VALUE] )
Delinquent Backlog $ = CALCULATE ( [Open Backlog $], VW_BACKLOG_CURRENT[IS_DELINQUENT] = TRUE () )
Delinquent % = DIVIDE ( [Delinquent Backlog $], [Open Backlog $] )

